# Scope guard for the automated AUR bump.
#
# The nightly `aur-bump.yml` workflow opens a PR that the vetting routine can
# merge without a human. That is only acceptable because the change is confined
# to vendored AUR PKGBUILDs. Two checks in the workflow already enforce that, but
# both live inside the thing being trusted -- this file moves the guarantee to
# GitHub, where neither the workflow nor the model can talk its way past it.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, and an entry with no owner clears ownership. So:
# everything requires the repo owner's review, except `aur/`, which the
# automation may merge on its own. A bump that somehow touched Containerfile.base
# or a workflow would need a human approval it cannot give itself.
#
# INERT WITHOUT A REPO SETTING. This file does nothing until branch protection on
# `main` enables "Require a pull request before merging" + "Require review from
# Code Owners". Leave "Do not allow bypassing" unchecked so admin pushes straight
# to main keep working; the restriction is meant for the automation, not for you.

